# EduTeams Project Structure

## Architecture Overview
EduTeams is a Next.js 15 application with TypeScript, Prisma, and Better Auth for team formation in educational settings.

## Key Directories
- `src/app/` - Next.js App Router pages and layouts
- `src/components/` - Reusable React components organized by feature
- `src/lib/` - Utility functions, API logic, and business logic
- `src/i18n/` - Internationalization (Indonesian/English)
- `prisma/` - Database schema and migrations
- `__tests__/` - Test files using Bun test runner

## Component Organization
- `components/auth/` - Authentication components
- `components/dashboard/` - Dashboard-specific components
- `components/onboarding/` - User onboarding flow components
- `components/ui/` - Reusable UI components (shadcn/ui based)

## File Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (e.g., `ClassCard.tsx`)
- Utilities: kebab-case (e.g., `api-utils.ts`)
- Pages: lowercase with hyphens (e.g., `page.tsx`)
- Tests: `*.test.ts` or `*.test.tsx`

## Import Patterns
- Use `@/` alias for src directory imports
- Group imports: external libraries, internal modules, relative imports
- Prefer named exports over default exports for utilities

## Key Files
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Dependencies and scripts
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) - TypeScript configuration
- [biome.json](mdc:biome.json) - Code formatting and linting
- [prisma/schema.prisma](mdc:prisma/schema.prisma) - Database schema
- [src/middleware.ts](mdc:src/middleware.ts) - Next.js middleware for auth